@startuml
title Record Exam Result

actor User
boundary "CertificationController" as Controller
control "CertificationApplicationService" as App
entity "CertificationRepository" as Repo
entity "Certification" as Certification

User -> Controller : POST /certifications/{id}/exam-results
Controller -> App : recordExamResult(command)
App -> Repo : findById(certificationId)
Repo --> App : Certification
App -> Certification : recordExamResult(examAttempt)
Certification -> Certification : append attempt
Certification -> Certification : update status
App -> Repo : save(certification)
Repo --> App : saved Certification
App --> Controller : result
Controller --> User : 200 OK

note right of Certification
Type:
Aggregate Root

Responsibility:
Own exam attempts and certification status.

Invariants:
ExamAttempt belongs to this Certification.
Passing result changes status to PASSED.

Persistence:
Saved with ExamAttempt children as one aggregate.
end note

note right of App
Type:
Application Service

Responsibility:
Coordinate loading, invoking domain behavior, and saving.

Business Rules:
Does not directly mutate status. Status change is handled by Certification.
end note

@enduml

